{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","version":"2.1.0","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"pmat"}},"results":[{"ruleId":"infra_assert_step_name_and_legacy_length_survive","level":"note","message":{"text":"Round-2 finding 1 is closed: infra_job and log_proves have rows, and m21, m22 and m25 kill the build-metadata strip, the completed/success check and the token-in-argv revert. Two small reviewer mutants still survive 69/69: (a) INFRA_ASSERT set to a wrong step name, because the infra_job row builds its fixture from the same variable, so a typo or an upstream rename of the step is not caught by any row (the lane then reads not_measured forever, conservative); (b) the legacy commit: record length bound {7,40} widened to {1,40}."},"properties":{"grounding":"measured","command":["bash","scripts/release/release_lanes.sh","--self-test"],"exit_code":0,"stdout_sha256":"0409de03f7bacdb9836b4eaf251b1205dcf3129f8548f10042814d8e93ec335a","failure_scenario":"On a copy with INFRA_ASSERT=x or {1,40}: 69 ok, 0 broke. If infra renames the assert step the cpu lane silently goes not_measured with the suite green.","precision_class":"advisory"}},{"ruleId":"tested_sha_legacy_only_log_reads_no_commit","level":"note","message":{"text":"Round-2 finding 3 is closed: the legacy commit: regex is byte-identical to cascade-publish.sh clean_room_tested_abbrevs (line 459), more than one record or a non-prefix of the structured sha proves no commit (m23, m24 kill the mutants). Remaining divergence, declared in the header: a log with only the legacy record reads as no commit where the driver resolves it with git. Conservative."},"properties":{"grounding":"cited","citation":"scripts/cascade-publish.sh:457-462","precision_class":"advisory"}},{"ruleId":"is_bumped_final_over_published_rc_reads_not_bumped","level":"note","message":{"text":"Round-2 finding 2, left as is by the author. Accepted: the operator rule is that crates.io receives only tagged FINALs, so a published rc of the next version cannot exist, and the direction is conservative (not_measured, never a false red or green)."},"properties":{"grounding":"asserted","rationale":"rests on the operator publication rule quoted in the coordinator message; not measurable from the tree.","precision_class":"advisory"}},{"ruleId":"complexity_not_measurable","level":"note","message":{"text":"pmat has no sh or yaml complexity analyzer; the delta is one shell file, so complexity_delta, tdg_delta and satd_introduced are empty by construction, not by a clean result. Own checks: --self-test 69 ok / 0 broke, --mutants 25/25 killed, check_bashrs_gate PASS."},"properties":{"grounding":"measured","command":["bash","scripts/release/release_lanes.sh","--mutants"],"exit_code":0,"stdout_sha256":"cdcd6de9fc49e51ea95581fb6c32eee315125eac204b55468617a46ffcee3b89","precision_class":"advisory"}}]},{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"antigravity"}},"results":[]}]}
